## Brief Overview

---

The hotel's own AV is usually the easier choice when your event fits what the room already has, such as a simple meeting with one screen and a microphone. An independent supplier makes sense when your event needs more than the room offers, when you want the same equipment and technician across several rooms or venues, or when you want the AV quoted separately so you can compare. Whichever you choose, get the equipment list, the technician's hours and the rules for outside suppliers in writing. Malaga Event Gear is an independent supplier: the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), at 490 euros ex VAT for up to 120 guests, includes delivery, installation and a technician for up to 6 hours.

## Key Highlights

---

-   The right answer depends on your event and on what the room already has. There is no rule that favors one side.
-   Ask the hotel what is installed in the room, who operates it, what it costs and whether outside suppliers are allowed.
-   Compare the same things in both quotes: equipment, technician hours, setup, teardown and extras.
-   An independent supplier still needs access, loading time, power and a contact at the hotel.
-   We are an independent supplier, and we make no claim about the equipment or the prices of any hotel.

-   **Who delivers it?** Our crew delivers, installs and tests the equipment. We work delivery only, with no self pickup.
-   **How much notice?** At least 24 hours, and as early as your dates are set for a congress.
-   **What is not covered?** The room, its installed equipment and anything outside our own inventory.

## What to Ask the Hotel

Before you compare anything, get the facts from the hotel. Ask for them in writing, because they settle most of the decision:

-   **What is installed in the room?** A ceiling projector, a screen, speakers, microphones, a mixing desk. Ask for a list, not a description.
-   **Who operates it?** Whether a technician is included, for how many hours and whether that person stays for the whole event.
-   **What does it cost?** The price of the equipment and of the technician, and what is included in the room price.
-   **Does the room contract require the hotel's AV?** Whether using the hotel's own equipment is a condition of the room booking.
-   **Are outside suppliers allowed?** Whether an independent company can bring its own equipment, and whether there is a fee or a rule for it.
-   **What are the rules for an outside supplier?** Access time, loading route, insurance, power points and the deadline to request them.

The answers tell you what you can use as it is and what you would have to add.

## When the Hotel's Own AV Is the Easier Choice

The hotel's own equipment is the simpler path in some cases:

-   **A small meeting.** One screen, one microphone and a short agenda fit what most meeting rooms already have.
-   **The installed system already does what you need.** If the room's projector, screen and speakers cover your program, you add nothing.
-   **One point of contact.** If the hotel runs the room, the equipment and the technician, you deal with one party.

In these cases an independent supplier adds a step. If the hotel's list covers your program and its quote is clear, using it is a reasonable decision.

## When an Independent Supplier Makes Sense

An independent supplier makes sense when the room does not cover your event, or when you want control over the AV:

-   **The room lacks something.** Microphones for a panel, a lectern, stage platforms, a second screen or more speakers than the room has.
-   **Several rooms or venues.** The same equipment and the same technician across your program, instead of a different setup in each room.
-   **A separate quote.** You want the AV priced on its own so you can compare it with another offer.
-   **A specific setup.** A speaker's rider that names a microphone or a monitor the room does not have. Our guide to [keynote speaker AV requirements](/blog/keynote-speaker-av-requirements/) shows what a main speaker usually asks for.

For a congress with a main hall and several parallel sessions, our guide on [how to organize a congress in Malaga](/blog/how-to-organize-a-congress-in-malaga/) puts the decisions in order, including when to write the audiovisual brief.

